<title>CANADA: Air Canada sees labor peace beyond holidays.</title>
<headline>Air Canada sees labor peace beyond holidays.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air Canada said on Monday that it expects a peaceful holiday season on the labor front if its sales and tickets agents approve a tentative agreement on a new contract.</p>
<p>&quot;Right now, we would face no labor disruption,&quot; Air Canada spokeswoman Kym Robertson told Reuters.</p>
<p>Earlier Monday, Air Canada said it had reached a tentative agreement with the Canadian Auto Workers representing the airline's 3,500 sales and ticket agents. The CAW said results of a country-wide membership ratification vote on the contract will be announced by December 19.</p>
</text>
